WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:01.420
Monster Party!

00:00:01.740 --> 00:00:03.100
It's a scream!

00:00:18.500 --> 00:00:26.460
And welcome to NEStalgia, a chronological exploration of every NES game released in North America.

00:00:26.680 --> 00:00:28.540
I'm Mike. And I'm Sean.

00:00:29.280 --> 00:00:36.360
Sean, it's just the two of us, and that's pretty spooky for the listeners, but not just because this is happening around Halloween time.

00:00:36.520 --> 00:00:42.160
It's just spooky to hear you and me knowing that we have complete control over the essential games list today.

00:00:42.480 --> 00:00:47.660
That's true, but that does also pose the quandary of there being a split.

00:00:48.020 --> 00:00:50.820
So I kind of forgot what happens then.

00:00:51.300 --> 00:00:52.840
I think nothing happens.

00:00:53.100 --> 00:00:54.140
Yeah, I think it just doesn't get on.

00:00:55.260 --> 00:00:56.380
That's kind of spooky.

00:00:56.380 --> 00:00:57.960
Yeah, we're agreeable guys.

00:00:58.320 --> 00:01:00.220
Yeah, I always say what you want me to say.

00:01:01.180 --> 00:01:02.360
Absolutely. Just read the script.

00:01:04.080 --> 00:01:05.720
Yes, I just read the script.

00:01:05.720 --> 00:01:06.760
Yep, there you go.

00:01:06.840 --> 00:01:09.060
It was line 31. Yes, I just read the script.

00:01:09.560 --> 00:01:12.980
Anyway, just in time for Halloween, we have Monster Party.

00:01:12.980 --> 00:01:29.880
I don't know if Nintendo knew that somebody was going to start a podcast around 2018, like in January, and that their games would sync up with games that are not being released around Halloween time, but somehow would sync up with their calendars for when they release the episodes of their podcast.

00:01:29.880 --> 00:01:31.560
But this is now twice in a row.

00:01:31.720 --> 00:01:32.620
That's pretty cool.

00:01:32.760 --> 00:01:38.440
We had Castlevania 2, Simon's Quest around Halloween last year, and now this time we have Monster Party.

00:01:38.740 --> 00:01:44.000
Of course, Monster Party is releasing in June of 1989, but none of this matters, right, Sean?

00:01:44.120 --> 00:01:46.180
Like, you don't really care when you buy a spooky game.

00:01:46.300 --> 00:01:47.400
It doesn't have to be in October.

00:01:47.400 --> 00:01:54.440
No, but like, you'll just, you'll play it a little bit in June, and then you'll definitely get in the mood again in October.

00:01:54.440 --> 00:01:56.820
It's all about the feel, you know?

00:01:57.700 --> 00:02:01.620
Yeah, and I would say Monster Party is definitely all about the feel.

00:02:01.960 --> 00:02:07.580
Going off the name alone, right, Monster Party, can you describe to me the kind of game you were expecting?

00:02:07.900 --> 00:02:10.580
Were you expecting anything off of this before you played it?

00:02:10.580 --> 00:02:21.340
I was correct in assuming that it was going to be about like vaguely horror themes, but I thought that the genre was going to be more of like a summer games sort of thing.

00:02:21.500 --> 00:02:28.660
It was going to be like a bunch of party games, but a universal movie monster themed.

00:02:28.960 --> 00:02:37.800
Yeah, Monster Party to me implies like, you know, you're going like level by level as the different like universal Hollywood monsters, you know?

00:02:37.800 --> 00:02:42.180
Also like one level, you're Frankenstein, one level, you're Dracula, the mummy, all that stuff.

00:02:42.440 --> 00:02:45.040
I mean, some of those characters are in this game, others are not.

00:02:45.440 --> 00:02:54.460
But Monster Party wasn't my idea of like playing as like this kid named Mark with a baseball bat being transported to hell.

00:02:54.720 --> 00:02:56.540
And his demon friend, Bert.

00:02:57.740 --> 00:03:01.060
Who tricks him into fusing bodies with him?

00:03:01.200 --> 00:03:03.300
Which I guess in some ways is like possession.

00:03:03.820 --> 00:03:06.600
Yeah, but okay, so let's just recap this for a minute, okay?

00:03:07.420 --> 00:03:08.340
Mark, right?

00:03:08.600 --> 00:03:10.340
The protagonist of the game.

00:03:10.620 --> 00:03:11.680
His name is just Mark.

00:03:11.840 --> 00:03:12.880
Not even anything that interesting.

00:03:13.160 --> 00:03:17.420
He's on his way home from what I got to believe is a baseball game because he has a baseball bat.

00:03:17.420 --> 00:03:18.920
It was indeed a baseball game.

00:03:19.720 --> 00:03:22.940
He's approached by this Griffin demon.

00:03:22.960 --> 00:03:24.560
Well, hold on. You're skipping.

00:03:25.140 --> 00:03:26.180
Okay, well, I didn't know if I needed to.

00:03:26.180 --> 00:03:29.940
He looks up into the sky and sees a star and then the star gets big.

00:03:29.940 --> 00:03:34.080
And he's also crying now because of how beautiful the night sky is.

00:03:34.240 --> 00:03:42.100
And then he realizes that the star had fallen in front of his feet and it was actually a monster all along.

00:03:42.680 --> 00:03:43.600
And that's Bert.

00:03:44.080 --> 00:03:45.320
And that's Bert, right.

00:03:45.440 --> 00:03:47.440
Who also just again like very normal name.

00:03:47.440 --> 00:03:51.360
I don't, you know, I guess Bert, Mark, they could be friends with each other.

00:03:51.540 --> 00:03:54.340
He's a very like affable guy too.

00:03:54.440 --> 00:03:56.100
He speaks pretty, like he's pretty friendly.

00:03:56.580 --> 00:03:58.860
Yeah, and you know he's familiar with the English language.

00:03:59.100 --> 00:04:03.680
Yeah. And he just kind of approaches and he's like, you know, hey, I'm Bert.

00:04:03.860 --> 00:04:05.220
And Mark's like, what's up?

00:04:05.560 --> 00:04:09.160
I just, something about that what's up is just classic.

00:04:09.360 --> 00:04:11.740
I'm not even making that up. That's literally what Mark says.

00:04:11.740 --> 00:04:12.800
I forgot about that.

00:04:13.440 --> 00:04:15.400
Yeah. He's like, he's like, yo, it's a demon.

00:04:15.620 --> 00:04:16.880
And the demon's like, I'm Bert.

00:04:17.000 --> 00:04:18.780
He's like, oh, what's up? What's up, Bert?

00:04:18.980 --> 00:04:22.820
It's like my world has been taken over by other demon evil things.

00:04:23.560 --> 00:04:24.680
I need you to help me.

00:04:25.080 --> 00:04:29.160
And then Mark's like, but I don't really have like anything to help you with there.

00:04:29.360 --> 00:04:31.060
Like I'm just a kid with a baseball bat.

00:04:31.220 --> 00:04:32.660
It's like, oh, that's fine.

00:04:33.560 --> 00:04:34.820
That's perfect. That'll do.

00:04:35.440 --> 00:04:36.460
Doesn't it seem odd though?

00:04:36.560 --> 00:04:40.880
Like Bert isn't also, he doesn't seem that convinced that the baseball bat's gonna work.

00:04:40.880 --> 00:04:42.860
He's like, oh, that's really all you have?

00:04:43.000 --> 00:04:43.960
Like, well, whatever.

00:04:44.200 --> 00:04:46.940
Like in the dark world, I'm sure a baseball bat will be fine.

00:04:47.120 --> 00:04:48.940
Like he seems like he's improvising.

00:04:49.180 --> 00:04:53.640
Yeah. I mean, but whether he's improvising or not, I think he's, he's not taking this seriously enough.

00:04:53.640 --> 00:04:59.260
If this boy, the baseball bat is all he thinks is gonna help him.

00:04:59.620 --> 00:05:10.800
Yeah. If you took the time to learn the English language from the dark world, you would think that you would like know about, you know, the world militaries or, you know, just like more important.

00:05:10.800 --> 00:05:14.540
Like more important people than nine year old Mark on his way home from baseball camp.

00:05:14.900 --> 00:05:23.160
Yeah. Or maybe, maybe he's speaking like a Bissell or, or some, or some demon language and Mark just hears it as English.

00:05:23.160 --> 00:05:28.480
So maybe he, he isn't really all that well versed in human behavior anyway.

00:05:28.480 --> 00:05:30.340
So they call it the dark world.

00:05:30.520 --> 00:05:36.900
Um, but at first it's not like, you know, I mean, I guess like the enemies are a little creepy and what have you, but it's not like too scary.

00:05:36.900 --> 00:05:43.740
And then there's just this moment within like the first minute of gameplay where the screw, the screen like glitches out.

00:05:43.740 --> 00:05:48.960
And then all of like, like all the trees have like faces and they're like, everything's bleeding.

00:05:49.640 --> 00:05:57.560
Yeah. It's, it's, it's just like a lot of, uh, gross out and blood and like, you know, weird enemies and stuff like that.

00:05:57.560 --> 00:06:02.220
And at this point you've got to assume that Bert tricked Mark into going to hell.

00:06:03.200 --> 00:06:05.900
I, I guess that's, that's one way to look at it.

00:06:06.000 --> 00:06:18.380
I will say that like, cause this is otherwise just, it starts out just as like a normal side scroller with the kind of like cut kind of good feeling, uh, controls.

00:06:18.380 --> 00:06:21.800
And he just got the baseball bat, he hit stuff with it.

00:06:22.180 --> 00:06:28.880
Um, but then that moment when that happens, uh, like it, that I think it really earned that moment.

00:06:28.880 --> 00:06:32.780
Like that was actually something that kind of freaked me out when it happened.

00:06:33.120 --> 00:06:36.900
Um, I don't know what your initial reaction was to that.

00:06:37.420 --> 00:06:45.560
Yeah. Well, I would say it freaked me out if only just because like the game becomes so much more graphic than you would expect from Nintendo.

00:06:46.020 --> 00:06:56.620
Yeah, exactly. Like, like you mentioned the blood on the faces and everything like that, but even like there's guys with just their like legs and asses sticking out from the ground.

00:06:57.100 --> 00:07:05.200
Yeah. And, and, um, dogs with human heads and, uh, fish with, with human legs.

00:07:05.200 --> 00:07:06.940
It's all, it's all very strange.

00:07:07.160 --> 00:07:11.660
Right. And don't forget that, you know, the, the members of the Beatles are walking around on fire too.

00:07:11.880 --> 00:07:13.460
They're just like, I guess the Beatles.

00:07:13.980 --> 00:07:16.140
Oh, that's, that's what you're saying.

00:07:16.140 --> 00:07:24.620
You meant, I was like, I don't remember the Beatle enemies, but, uh, you know, it's like these English looking guys who kind of look like, you know, what makes them look British or yeah, I don't.

00:07:24.660 --> 00:07:26.340
It's the haircut. I don't.

00:07:26.500 --> 00:07:33.140
Okay. So you're talking about the, the, the black beings that kind of look there like they're also on fire.

00:07:33.560 --> 00:07:34.880
Oh, they're definitely on fire.

00:07:35.060 --> 00:07:37.220
Okay. They look British to you.

00:07:37.220 --> 00:07:45.100
You don't think that they look like they're dressed like, you know, like an alternate outfit of Sergeant Pepper's Lonely Hearts Club Band or something.

00:07:45.360 --> 00:07:47.100
Like. I would say they don't look like they're dressed.

00:07:47.100 --> 00:07:49.220
I feel like we're looking at their charred skin.

00:07:49.220 --> 00:07:51.760
It's very, it's very unsettling.

00:07:52.160 --> 00:07:53.040
Except for that.

00:07:53.260 --> 00:07:54.540
We can see that they have a face.

00:07:54.540 --> 00:07:59.720
So I'm thinking that that's their hair, that black stuff, you know, like you can see a face a little bit.

00:07:59.800 --> 00:08:00.780
Right. You see that?

00:08:00.940 --> 00:08:02.160
Like. I don't actually.

00:08:02.160 --> 00:08:03.780
I don't think that's your skin under the, okay.

00:08:03.920 --> 00:08:11.420
Yeah. Anyway, I'm getting pretty into it, but I was surprised to see the Beatles in the, in the game.

00:08:11.560 --> 00:08:12.980
I guess it's a Rorschach test.

00:08:13.140 --> 00:08:15.480
You just got to watch out for the Beatles is all I'm saying.

00:08:15.700 --> 00:08:17.620
Yeah. Because they'll, they'll be there waiting for you in hell.

00:08:17.660 --> 00:08:20.180
But everything has a face in this game all of a sudden.

00:08:20.180 --> 00:08:26.080
It's like every, every tree has a face, but also every leaf on a tree has a face.

00:08:26.320 --> 00:08:28.820
Every block has a, has a skull.

00:08:28.820 --> 00:08:35.560
Um, I, I'm pretty sure like there's no shortage of, of just like body horror in this game.

00:08:35.560 --> 00:08:37.840
You've got like half fish, half man.

00:08:38.080 --> 00:08:40.720
You've got eyeballs with tentacles for feet.

00:08:40.940 --> 00:08:45.500
There's just like a lot of graphic stuff going on here and I'm digging it.

00:08:45.740 --> 00:08:52.360
Yeah. I, I really liked the aesthetic that they went for here, even though it's, um, kind of goofy

00:08:52.360 --> 00:08:54.020
if you take anything out of context.

00:08:54.020 --> 00:09:01.460
But for some reason when everything is this, uh, this eight bit horror look, it all really

00:09:01.460 --> 00:09:04.180
works together. Um, yeah.

00:09:05.360 --> 00:09:09.480
Right. Cause you know, it's also, like you said, it's a side scrolling platforming game.

00:09:09.680 --> 00:09:15.580
So, um, you know, there's like a, there's a way that we're used to playing those games

00:09:15.580 --> 00:09:19.580
because they're, they're pretty easy to make after Super Mario Brothers laying down the ground,

00:09:19.580 --> 00:09:21.340
uh, the blueprints and stuff like that.

00:09:21.460 --> 00:09:27.320
But this game is, has pretty good controls like overall, like, yeah, it could do with

00:09:27.320 --> 00:09:30.960
maybe like your baseball bat having a little more powers as we don't have to constantly

00:09:30.960 --> 00:09:33.400
attack enemies as they continue to move towards you.

00:09:33.580 --> 00:09:38.220
But for the most part, like it's pretty, it feels pretty good to navigate around this stage

00:09:38.220 --> 00:09:39.360
and fight these enemies.

00:09:39.360 --> 00:09:42.160
And they're not, they're not like littering the screen with them.

00:09:42.160 --> 00:09:48.820
So it's more of just like taking in the world and, and being in this world that is like

00:09:48.820 --> 00:09:53.020
the shocking part of the game and not like making your way through the levels.

00:09:53.160 --> 00:09:54.320
Right. Yeah.

00:09:54.520 --> 00:10:00.160
And one of the thing that I I'd like to note about this game is like when, when we talk

00:10:00.160 --> 00:10:09.360
about how, um, one note, I guess, or how much of the design of this game is just its

00:10:09.360 --> 00:10:13.260
theme and how it really leans into its theme for everything.

00:10:13.660 --> 00:10:18.620
Like when I think of games like that now, or in a lot of like, I don't know, like PS1

00:10:18.620 --> 00:10:22.820
era games, like that was really the only thing that was unique about it.

00:10:23.100 --> 00:10:29.380
Um, it was just a reskin of a game you had played dozens and dozens of times, but, um,

00:10:29.760 --> 00:10:36.780
this game has enough unique game mechanics, uh, like especially using your baseball bat that

00:10:36.780 --> 00:10:45.300
it doesn't feel just like a horror version of Mario or a horror version of, uh, some other

00:10:46.080 --> 00:10:47.040
side scroller.

00:10:47.320 --> 00:10:52.460
It actually has like a fully formed design.

00:10:53.400 --> 00:10:54.420
Right. Yeah.

00:10:54.500 --> 00:10:59.320
I mean, yeah. Like you said about that baseball bat, like it can even deflect projectiles if you hit with

00:10:59.320 --> 00:11:00.460
the baseball bat at the right time.

00:11:00.540 --> 00:11:04.400
Which is a very, it's used a lot that like the whole bosses are about that.

00:11:04.400 --> 00:11:08.880
The blueprints of a good game are here for the overall objective though.

00:11:09.020 --> 00:11:11.320
It's not just about getting from left to right, right?

00:11:11.400 --> 00:11:15.500
There's no like goalposts that you have to clear or, you know, end of stage walk through.

00:11:15.780 --> 00:11:19.880
There are these doors that are just everywhere inside the levels.

00:11:20.240 --> 00:11:22.620
And some of them have boss fights.

00:11:22.740 --> 00:11:25.360
Some of them have, uh, nothing.

00:11:25.600 --> 00:11:26.580
Nothing is an option.

00:11:26.780 --> 00:11:28.920
You could just walk into a room and have to leave it.

00:11:28.920 --> 00:11:33.180
And then others have like, you know, small enemies or puzzles or something like that.

00:11:33.220 --> 00:11:34.840
I don't think there's actually any puzzles, but like.

00:11:34.980 --> 00:11:35.960
There's a dance sequence.

00:11:36.320 --> 00:11:39.940
Yeah. The dance sequence, uh, just different things happen behind these doors.

00:11:39.960 --> 00:11:41.580
I guess is the point I'm trying to get across.

00:11:41.760 --> 00:11:47.660
But ultimately the goal is to find a key that you then take to the end of the level.

00:11:48.080 --> 00:11:50.080
And it's not really finding a key.

00:11:50.320 --> 00:11:52.180
It's really just clearing everything.

00:11:52.180 --> 00:11:55.900
Like you don't get the key until you fight the bosses.

00:11:56.140 --> 00:12:01.000
If like, if there are multiple and you grab all the question marks, I think.

00:12:01.980 --> 00:12:03.580
I believe you're right there.

00:12:03.580 --> 00:12:08.060
But also like, you know, doesn't that just make the point of the key kind of silly?

00:12:08.300 --> 00:12:10.700
Like, shouldn't we just have it be that you have to.

00:12:10.940 --> 00:12:12.480
I think it's more just like.

00:12:12.780 --> 00:12:13.900
The bosses of the stage. Yeah.

00:12:13.980 --> 00:12:17.120
It should just say clear and then say yes.

00:12:17.980 --> 00:12:24.780
Right. You know, I think like just something, it seems like the key thing is just the added element of being like, make sure you do.

00:12:24.920 --> 00:12:26.260
Like you have the choice, right?

00:12:26.400 --> 00:12:29.000
Like you do it in whatever order you feel like.

00:12:29.200 --> 00:12:34.300
But there's really no reason to go like all the way to the end of the stage and go to a door there.

00:12:34.620 --> 00:12:37.520
And then go back track and go to another door.

00:12:37.660 --> 00:12:40.460
You're better off just attacking the doors in sequence.

00:12:40.660 --> 00:12:42.340
Right. Unless I'm missing something.

00:12:42.420 --> 00:12:46.160
I mean, yeah. Power ups or hidden things that you need to get first.

00:12:46.160 --> 00:12:50.620
Yeah, I would say that you're definitely correct there.

00:12:51.500 --> 00:12:55.880
I remember missing one and kind of not understanding what the key was.

00:12:56.040 --> 00:12:59.160
But that was just because I found a couple empties.

00:12:59.300 --> 00:13:01.160
And I'm like, oh, I guess I don't have to go into these.

00:13:03.120 --> 00:13:05.460
So that can be a little unclear.

00:13:05.640 --> 00:13:09.480
But after you realize that, oh, I just have to go into everything.

00:13:09.860 --> 00:13:11.620
You don't run into that problem anymore.

00:13:12.180 --> 00:13:13.540
Right. And so it's like the game.

00:13:13.660 --> 00:13:15.120
The gameplay is pretty solid.

00:13:15.120 --> 00:13:19.700
It's the tediousness of going through the doors, knowing that you have to go through all of them, too.

00:13:19.820 --> 00:13:23.800
You don't get to like skip a door because you need to go through all the doors.

00:13:24.000 --> 00:13:26.720
It's like that objective is just a little strange.

00:13:26.720 --> 00:13:30.180
And it's also not clear from like from what Bert was telling you.

00:13:30.320 --> 00:13:35.660
Right. Like I wouldn't know that, you know, like you said, you you miss a door and you didn't realize what the keys were about.

00:13:36.480 --> 00:13:38.380
So that's just that's just the way it is.

00:13:39.700 --> 00:13:41.900
It's you know, it's not like the end of the world for me.

00:13:41.980 --> 00:13:44.840
I'm not saying I can't play this game because getting the key is really hard.

00:13:44.840 --> 00:13:57.160
Just a noticeable difference between what should have maybe just been like get through the level to fight, you know, the mid boss and then the final boss of the stage or whatever to progress on might have been a little.

00:13:58.880 --> 00:14:01.280
It isn't it is an added contrivance.

00:14:01.540 --> 00:14:02.520
Right. Exactly.

00:14:02.900 --> 00:14:08.020
And I feel like the boss fights in the game are are an element of their own.

00:14:08.100 --> 00:14:24.780
Right. Like so the bosses are all like really unique looking and like some of them are like clearly based on horror movies, but others are like just a just a Halloween esque thing like that pumpkin guy that you fight.

00:14:25.040 --> 00:14:26.860
Don't pick on me. Yeah.

00:14:27.020 --> 00:14:29.120
Don't pick on me. But they all say something weird, too.

00:14:29.120 --> 00:14:33.760
The bosses definitely are their own thing because every boss says they have a one liner strange.

00:14:34.180 --> 00:14:36.160
Yeah. Who was your favorite?

00:14:37.040 --> 00:14:38.180
Sorry, I'm dead.

00:14:38.340 --> 00:14:39.260
And he's not even a boss.

00:14:39.400 --> 00:14:40.720
But I thought that was really funny.

00:14:40.920 --> 00:14:44.540
That was actually also like it could have been scary.

00:14:44.780 --> 00:14:49.240
And if you were playing it in the right context, it's just so unexpected.

00:14:49.820 --> 00:14:57.760
And like when it's unexpected and also kind of underwhelming for like in a horror setting.

00:14:58.180 --> 00:14:59.180
It's kind of eerie.

00:14:59.340 --> 00:15:01.280
I don't know if you know what I mean there.

00:15:02.880 --> 00:15:03.700
Well, yeah. No.

00:15:03.820 --> 00:15:06.220
So it's like that's another thing where it's like mood building, though.

00:15:06.280 --> 00:15:08.940
So I could imagine if you're in like Silent Hill.

00:15:09.140 --> 00:15:12.480
Right. You go into a room and somebody says, sorry, I'm dead.

00:15:12.620 --> 00:15:15.860
Like that is scary and has like a sense of dread to it.

00:15:15.860 --> 00:15:22.980
But this game can't quite reach that level of like of scare, you know, like where I think I see sorry, I'm dead.

00:15:23.100 --> 00:15:27.420
And I can't help but like laugh, you know, it's too colorful of a game.

00:15:27.480 --> 00:15:29.060
I know. Still like live in that world.

00:15:29.140 --> 00:15:31.820
But you're right. It does teeter that line a little bit.

